# `cargo clippy --locked --tests -j2`, counting real diagnostic warnings —
# cargo's own per-target "generated N warnings" summary lines are excluded so a
# warning is never counted twice.
#
# Split per crate because they are separate cargo invocations: a root-only
# clippy run never lints apps/desktop/src-tauri, which is the same blind spot
# that let that crate ship un-compilable twice.
#
# MEASURED 2026-07-30 on a clean tranche/6 tree, fresh target dir, exit 0 both.
# The "80" and "83" figures circulating in docs/release/v0.6/ could not be
# reproduced by any counting method against this command; docs/architecture/
# testing.md contradicts them again by documenting `-- -D warnings`, which
# cannot be passing at any non-zero baseline. All three are stale. These two
# numbers are what the command actually produces.
#
# ROOT TIGHTENED 76 -> 75 on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 verification sweep. This
# is a CEILING, so the safe direction is DOWN and this is debt being paid, not
# a floor being dropped: the SD-27 work removed one warning at source and the
# run reported `ceiling is loose: 76 recorded, 75 measured`. Leaving 76 in
# place would silently re-license the warning that was just fixed. Desktop is
# unchanged at 7.
#
# BOTH HELD AGAIN, UNCHANGED, on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 tranche/7-1
# RE-verification sweep, over a tree that had since gained the feat-effects
# seam, the Wizard known-spell gate and feat prerequisite enforcement:
# `PASS clippy (root:75 desktop:7 warnings, 0 errors)`, exactly the ceilings,
# no "ceiling is loose" note. Three code-bearing changes landed without adding
# a single lint, so there was nothing to raise and nothing to pay down.
#
# BOTH HELD, UNCHANGED, on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 tranche/7-1 verification
# sweep: measured 75 root / 7 desktop on a fully settled tree carrying all
# three agents' diffs, i.e. exactly the ceilings, with the stage PASSING and
# no "ceiling is loose" note. Nothing was raised and nothing could be lowered.
#
# This also settles a dispute between two agents, by measurement rather than
# by argument: one reported desktop clippy as "really 18, not 7". It is 7 when
# counted the way THIS FILE's contract says and the way `clippy_one_crate`
# actually counts -- `cargo clippy --locked --tests`, `^warning:` lines with
# cargo's per-target "generated N warnings" summaries excluded. The 18 came
# from `--all-targets` piped through `grep -c '^warning'`, which both widens
# the target set and re-counts the summary lines the contract excludes. The
# counter-correction was right; the ceiling stands at 7.
#
# BOTH HELD AGAIN, UNCHANGED, on 2026-07-31 by the SD-27 tranche/7-1
# REACH-CLOSURE verification sweep, over a tree that had since gained the
# flat-footed-AC engine seam, the ARG automatic-grant resolver pass, the APG
# `.COPY=` spell resolution, a whole new `monster_catalog.rs` + React screen,
# and the PU per-corpus-key reach claim: `PASS clippy (root:75 desktop:7
# warnings, 0 errors)`, exactly the ceilings, with no "ceiling is loose" note.
# Five code-bearing changes across BOTH crates landed without adding a single
# lint, so there was nothing to raise and nothing to pay down.
BASELINE_CLIPPY_WARNINGS_ROOT=75
BASELINE_CLIPPY_WARNINGS_DESKTOP=7

